    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build is green. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Change: structured address form\n\nThe request now accepts a structured address (`addressLine1`, optional `addressLine2`, `city`, `postcode`) alongside the legacy flat `address`, preferring the structured fields when present while staying backward-compatible.\n\n**Where each piece of logic went:**\n\n- **`openapi.yml` (request/response contract)** \u2014 Added `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` to the `OwnerFields` schema, dropped `address` from the `required` list and removed its `@NotBlank` (so structured-only owners validate), and attached a new class-level `@ValidAddress` alongside the existing `@ValidPostcode`. Since these live in `OwnerFields`, the structured fields and the composed `address` flow through to the `Owner` response automatically.\n\n- **`ValidAddress` + `AddressFormValidator`** (new, mirroring the postcode pair) \u2014 A small class-level constraint enforcing \"an address in either form\": valid when `addressLine1` is non-blank *or* the flat `address` is present. `city` stays covered by its own `@NotBlank`.\n\n- **`OwnerMapper.composeAddress(...)`** \u2014 The single place that resolves the canonical `address`: normalized `addressLine1`, with a single space and normalized `addressLine2` appended when present, else the normalized flat `address`. `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` are also normalized and stored. Because everything downstream (household hash, postcode validation, locality) reads the one composed `address`/shared `city`/`postcode`, behavior stays consistent whichever form was supplied. Reuses the existing `AddressNormalizer` \u2014 no duplicated normalization rules.\n\n- **`Owner` entity + all four DB schemas** \u2014 Added `address_line1`/`address_line2` columns and accessors.\n\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.updateOwner`** \u2014 Reuses the same mapper helpers so the update path composes/normalizes identically to create (it previously stored the raw address).\n\n**Test results:** `coreNormalizesAndComposesStructuredAddress` and `functionalityStillAcceptsFlatAddress` both pass; full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
